@article{Aab2015Pierre,
  abstract = {The Pierre Auger Observatory, located on a vast, high plain in western Argentina, is the world's largest cosmic ray observatory. The objectives of the Observatory are to probe the origin and characteristics of cosmic rays above 1017 eV and to study the interactions of these, the most energetic particles observed in nature. The Auger design features an array of 1660 water Cherenkov particle detector stations spread over 3000 km2 overlooked by 24 air fluorescence telescopes. In addition, three high elevation fluorescence telescopes overlook a 23.5 km2, 61-detector infilled array with 750 m spacing. The Observatory has been in successful operation since completion in 2008 and has recorded data from an exposure exceeding 40,000 km2 sr yr. This paper describes the design and performance of the detectors, related subsystems and infrastructure that make up the Observatory.},
  author = {A. Aab and P. Abreu and M. Aglietta and E. J. Ahn and I. Al Samarai and J. N. Albert and I. F.M. Albuquerque and I. Allekotte and J. Allen and P. Allison and A. Almela and J. Alvarez Castillo and J. Alvarez-Muñiz and R. Alves Batista and M. Ambrosio and A. Aminaei and L. Anchordoqui and S. Andringa and C. Aramo and V. M. Aranda and S. Argirò and K. Arisaka and F. Arneodo and F. Arqueros and T. Asch and H. Asorey and P. Assis and J. Aublin and M. Ave and M. Avenier and G. Avila and N. Awal and A. M. Badescu and M. Balzer and K. B. Barber and A. Barbosa and N. Barenthien and J. Bäuml and C. Baus and J. J. Beatty and K. H. Becker and J. A. Bellido and S. BenZvi and C. Berat and T. Bergmann and M. E. Bertaina and P. L. Biermann and R. Bilhaut and P. Billoir and S. G. Blaess and M. Blanco and C. Bleve and H. Blümer and M. Boháčová and H. Bolz and D. Boncioli and C. Bonifazi and R. Bonino and M. Boratav and N. Borodai and F. Bracci and J. Brack and I. Brancus and A. Bridgeman and P. Brogueira and W. C. Brown and P. Buchholz and A. Bueno and S. Buitink and M. Buscemi and K. S. Caballero-Mora and B. Caccianiga and L. Caccianiga and D. Camin and M. Candusso and L. Caramete and R. Caruso and A. Castellina and A. Castera and G. Cataldi and L. Cazon and R. Cester and A. G. Chavez and A. Chiavassa and J. A. Chinellato and M. Chiosso and J. Chudoba and M. Cilmo and P. D.J. Clark and R. W. Clay and G. Cocciolo and R. Colalillo and A. Coleman and L. Collica and E. Colombo and S. Colonges and M. R. Coluccia and R. Conceiçáo and F. Contreras and M. J. Cooper and J. Coppens and A. Cordier and B. Courty and S. Coutu and C. E. Covault and J. Cronin and A. Curutiu and R. Dallier and B. Daniel and S. Dasso and K. Daumiller and B. R. Dawson and R. M. De Almeida and M. De Domenico and C. De Donato and S. J. De Jong and J. R.T. De Mello Neto and I. De Mitri and J. De Oliveira and V. De Souza and K. D. De Vries and L. Del Peral and O. Deligny and H. Dembinski and N. Dhital and C. 